<!-- Detailed Program Sections with IDs for Direct Navigation -->
<section class="sec sec--band" id="downwinders">
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <div style="max-width:880px;margin:0 auto;width:100%">
      <span class="pill">Highlighted Category</span>
      <h2 style="margin-top:8px">1. Downwinders Program ($100,000)</h2>
      <p class="lede">Between 1951 and 1962, the U.S. government conducted approximately 100 above-ground nuclear weapons tests at the Nevada Test Site. Radioactive fallout drifted across neighboring communities.</p>
      
      <div class="notice" style="margin-top:var(--sp2)">
        <h3>Covered Residency Guidelines</h3>
        <p>A claimant must have been physically present in a covered area for at least <strong>one continuous year</strong> between January 21, 1951 and November 6, 1962, OR for the entire month of <strong>July 1962</strong> (June 30 to July 31, 1962). For New Mexico, presence qualifies beginning September 24, 1944.</p>
        <table>
          <tr><th scope="row" style="width:200px">Statewide</th><td>Utah, New Mexico, Idaho (Entire states covered)</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Arizona</th><td>Apache, Coconino, Gila, Mohave, Navajo, Yavapai counties</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Nevada</th><td>Eureka, Lander, Lincoln, Nye, White Pine, and designated portions of Clark County</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top:var(--sp2)"><strong>Covered Illnesses:</strong> Leukemia (except CLL), Multiple Myeloma, Lymphomas, Breast Cancer, Thyroid Cancer, Lung Cancer, Stomach Cancer, Colon Cancer, Brain Cancer, Urinary Bladder, Pancreas, Ovary, and other primary malignancies.</p>

      <div class="btns" style="margin-top:var(--sp2)">
        <a class="btn" href="/check/">Check Downwinder Eligibility</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="onsite">
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <div style="max-width:880px;margin:0 auto;width:100%">
      <h2>2. On-Site Participants ($100,000)</h2>
      <p class="lede">Veterans and civilian workers who were stationed or present at nuclear detonations are eligible for federal compensation if they developed a covered cancer.</p>
      <p>This includes atmospheric nuclear tests at the Nevada Test Site, Pacific test sites (Operation Crossroads, Ivy, Castle, Redwing, Hardtack), and related military maneuvers.</p>
      <div class="btns" style="margin-top:var(--sp2)">
        <a class="btn" href="/check/">Check On-Site Eligibility</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec sec--band" id="uranium">
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <div style="max-width:880px;margin:0 auto;width:100%">
      <h2>3. Uranium Miners, Millers &amp; Ore Transporters ($100,000)</h2>
      <p class="lede">Uranium workers were exposed to heavy radon progeny and radioactive dust. Unlike other programs, coverage is not restricted to cancer.</p>
      <div class="notice" style="margin-top:var(--sp2)">
        <h3>Covered Non-Cancer &amp; Cancer Illnesses</h3>
        <p>Primary Lung Cancer, Silicosis, Pulmonary Fibrosis, Pneumoconiosis, Cor Pulmonale, Renal (Kidney) Cancer, and Chronic Renal Disease (including nephritis).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="btns" style="margin-top:var(--sp2)">
        <a class="btn" href="/check/">Check Uranium Eligibility</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="manhattan">
